<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5a6ed1cb790839e8773f6c3761e6c501a2041e0d" commit="9ad43c34f494393e1326da4758c13f4e0c86a49d" commit_message="dome: front-end: add TaskList component  The TaskList component may need to be reused in other pages in the future (such as the WelcomePage), so separate it from the AppPage to make it reusable.  BUG=b:30999924 TEST=Manually tested  Change-Id: I5a6ed1cb790839e8773f6c3761e6c501a2041e0d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384191 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384191" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/91/384191/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7b5914fefdfd089c7d831c8f52ffdbff13061e90" commit="b705a6f71092311846adc026668469c48f319e10" commit_message="dome: set maximum process to 1 in uwsgi.ini  This is the lazy way to make sure no racing condition will happen. Say, if we made a change to bundle A, Dome stages the Umpire config, tries to update, and deploy. If we tried to make a change to bundle B before task A finishes, task B won't be able to stage the config since it's already staged, thus, task B will definitely fail. We can implement a synchronization mechanism in the back-end, but that would take some effort, let's just make it 1 unless we really need to increase performance.  BUG=b:30999924 TEST=Manually tested  Change-Id: I7b5914fefdfd089c7d831c8f52ffdbff13061e90 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384273 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384273" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/73/384273/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I016178f24c87b17ef27390b21787410c55191c12" commit="11baae39aeb197ccdb74e22e69c13cfe07b4695b" commit_message="dome: fix a bug that Umpire does not actually get files uploaded by Dome  Uploaded files are stored in /tmp by default, which is not shared between Dome and Umpire Docker containers currently. Therefore, Umpire cannot see uploaded files from Dome.  A coincidence is that we forgot to remove the factory toolkit file used when setting up a new Umpire container. The file was left in the container. Every time we updated factory toolkit, the Umpire container read that old file instead of the new file we uploaded, creating an illusion that the update succeeded while it's not.  This patch also works around b/31415816 in which the temporary files were not removed immediately after finished requests.  BUG=b:31417203,b:31415816,b:30999924 TEST=Manually tested  Change-Id: I016178f24c87b17ef27390b21787410c55191c12 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384095 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384095" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/95/384095/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia7832f00194657ac62ffd9d34e9191e7c043ea3c" commit="27a90eb76a423c68a043cef7118b5c35249f0932" commit_message="dome: front-end: allow only one task running at the same time  In order to provide the cancel function, we need to queue tasks. Tasks are executed one-by-one, tasks on the waiting list are cancellable (tasks that finished and running are not cancellable).  This patch doesn't implement the cancel function but implements the queue mechanism (so we can implement cancel function in the future).  BUG=b:30999924 TEST=Manually tested  Change-Id: Ia7832f00194657ac62ffd9d34e9191e7c043ea3c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384272 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384272" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/72/384272/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id1d6a22c9738d87ddb416923e41c44dfd587f774" commit="d74417b0891b31acf1399451de46d639ec808fd7" commit_message="dome: front-end: rephrase the description of tasks  Also fix a bug that task list may not keep its order after dismiss one of the task.  BUG=b:30999924 TEST=Manaully tested  Change-Id: Id1d6a22c9738d87ddb416923e41c44dfd587f774 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384395 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384395" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/95/384395/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7f696166a351fee4230b066ca2ab204562f2c45e" commit="cbbf28291f77d4170087dbd6e22704e018b58f02" commit_message="dome: front-end: refactor constant files  Move all constants into export default so we don't have to write them twice.  BUG=b:30999924 TEST=Manually tested  Change-Id: I7f696166a351fee4230b066ca2ab204562f2c45e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384279 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384279" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/79/384279/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I59d9dab3e2907c1c2a32d24dc3ba20c7d65c279d" commit="20194ca4797716bc081d8367fe9d5f2495d13586" commit_message="libchromeos-ui: switch to a USE flag to disable flash low latency audio  We want to kill of IsBoard, so switch these guys to a USE flag.  BUG=chromium:407731 TEST=None CQ-DEPEND=CL:384412,CL:384771  Change-Id: I59d9dab3e2907c1c2a32d24dc3ba20c7d65c279d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384472 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384472" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/72/384472/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia004085b59172accc60ebbd5c22ea4619b8a47e0" commit="f4134a1404326fe5248a90393854348b6d3173a5" commit_message="libchromeos-use-flags: add USE=disable_low_latency_audio  This is used to control flash low latency audio behavior instead of looking at the board name.  BUG=chromium:407731 TEST=None CQ-DEPEND=CL:384472,CL:384412  Change-Id: Ia004085b59172accc60ebbd5c22ea4619b8a47e0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384771 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384771" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/71/384771/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I16d49a5087408c2fc2af1e679d481c3edbc41006" commit="f4107574c96302c298fbaab723d332260655bdd8" commit_message="alex/mario/zgb: add USE=disable_low_latency_audio  This controls the flash flag for turning of low latency audio. It's already disabled, but we're just turning it from being based on the board name to a USE flag.  BUG=chromium:407731 TEST=None CQ-DEPEND=CL:384771,CL:384472  Change-Id: I16d49a5087408c2fc2af1e679d481c3edbc41006 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384412 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384412" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/12/384412/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="Idea6acaf7e554d84c2030d6ea945476357a92bf2" commit="67aed4a9e96d0a338fd5bc8be44fe913f32ab88e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/exynos: remove remnants of GEM CPU acquire/release ioctls  BUG=none TEST=compile and install kernel 3.8 and run webgl aquarium  Change-Id: Idea6acaf7e554d84c2030d6ea945476357a92bf2 Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384363 " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="384363" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/63/384363/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I102294b88ba8e3c80e27b0fd7b40ba51c6da5886" commit="50b894b2e011b7cfea57b89bf79ddb4a5fe5d69b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: rockchip: Flip assigned clock orders in VOPs  The VOPs specify some assigned clock rates for their clocks in their device tree node.  Specifically: * ACLK / HCLK: Nobody sets these rates but they need to be sane. * DCLK: This is the pixel clock and will eventually be set, but needs to   be at a sane rate during init time.  It appears that when we set these clocks up the order is quite important, partially due to some of the hacks we have in http://crosreview.com/362820.  Specifically:  1. At boot (if firmware doesn't touch) then ACLK, HCLK, and DCLK for    VOP0 are all parented on VPLL. 2. Due to our hacks to the clock framework, when we change the DCLK we    allow it to change VPLL to suit its needs. 3. If we change DCLK first then the ACLK and HCLK will temporarily have    a screwy clock rate.  Let's avoid these problems by specifying the ACLK / HCLK first (which should cause them to reparent to another PLL) and _then_ change DPLL (which should change VPLL).  It's still a little unclear why glitching the clock rate of ACLK / HCLK causes so many problems, but this definitely seems to avoid them.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57351 TEST=Boot w/ gbb flags of 0x0 and see no hang.  Change-Id: I102294b88ba8e3c80e27b0fd7b40ba51c6da5886 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384299 Reviewed-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384299" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/99/384299/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I734806fb9219998ef38feaecacf535ea6b698a74" commit="c986bbcf638d7c7021f1c4fb431ca3676565252c" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: rockchip: set kevin digitizer delay to 100ms  Wacom has recommended 100ms delay, not the approximate 40ms we guessed. In practice, this seems to be well more than plenty, but let's do it anyway.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56993 TEST=suspend/resume kevin, test digitizer  Change-Id: I734806fb9219998ef38feaecacf535ea6b698a74 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384454 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="384454" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/54/384454/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I123fbd0658b8d4b889eabc093e2e32c25c7c998a" commit="aa27a50146ada2c46da6b473482bf960e8e6c185" commit_message="goofy: connection_manager: fix connect to WLAN  When goofy is trying to communicate with shill using dbus-python, and introspect gives no result about method signature, it would guess the type to use if no signature is given. For dictionary type, it would use an arbitrary entry in it, and use its type as the type of all entries.  Since the org.chromium.flimflam.Manager interface seems to be not introspectable, and we have both boolean and string as dictionary values, we need to explicitly specify the signature.  BUG=chromium:645870 TEST=manual  Change-Id: I123fbd0658b8